        "narrative": "<p>This lake has good populations of lake trout, northern pike, and white sucker, and some yellow perch and burbot.  All fish are naturally produced and populations are self-sustaining.The number and size of lake trout caught in this assessment were within the usual range for this class of lake.  Fish of ages 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, and 9 were identified in the sample, indicating consistent natural reproduction.  Growth of lake trout had been slower than the average for the lake class.  Northern pike collected appeared to be no older than age 3, but had grown quickly, and some large individuals were present.</p>",
